# Committing changes

Only commit or push when the user asks. Never edit `CHANGELOG.md` by hand.

1. Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject` (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`).
2. Commit the work. If the user asked to commit separately / by scope, follow `.cursor/skills/commit-separately/SKILL.md` (one commit per part, then changelog). If the user asked to release, bump the version, or fold Unreleased into a version, follow `.cursor/skills/release/SKILL.md`.
3. Run `make changelog`.
4. If `CHANGELOG.md` changed, commit `chore(changelog): regenerate from commits`.
5. Then push, and only if the user asked. A release request includes push and tag.

The pre-push hook and CI fail on a stale changelog. `chore(changelog)` commits are omitted from the file so regeneration does not loop.
